{
  "parents": [],
  "prev": {
    "link": "../",
    "title": "Reckon Python API"
  },
  "next": {
    "link": "../memory/",
    "title": "Memory API"
  },
  "title": "Core API",
  "meta": null,
  "body": "<section id=\"core-api\">\n<h1>Core API<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#core-api\" title=\"Link to this heading\">¶</a></h1>\n<section id=\"module-reckon.core.resources\">\n<span id=\"resources\"></span><h2>Resources<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-reckon.core.resources\" title=\"Link to this heading\">¶</a></h2>\n<p>Resource vectors and memory budgets.</p>\n<p>Defines the multi-dimensional resource constraints under which agents operate.</p>\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.resources.ResourceVector\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">reckon.core.resources.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">ResourceVector</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">memory_slots</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">memory_bytes</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">memory_tokens</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">bandwidth</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">compute</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">noise_floor</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.resources.ResourceVector\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>A multi-dimensional resource constraint vector.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Variables<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>memory_slots</strong> (<em>int | None</em>) – Maximum number of memory slots</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>memory_bytes</strong> (<em>int | None</em>) – Maximum memory in bytes</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>memory_tokens</strong> (<em>int | None</em>) – Maximum memory in tokens</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>bandwidth</strong> (<em>float | None</em>) – Maximum bandwidth (ops/step)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>compute</strong> (<em>float | None</em>) – Maximum compute per step</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>noise_floor</strong> (<em>float</em>) – Irreducible noise level</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>memory_slots</strong> (<em>int | None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>memory_bytes</strong> (<em>int | None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>memory_tokens</strong> (<em>int | None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>bandwidth</strong> (<em>float | None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>compute</strong> (<em>float | None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>noise_floor</strong> (<em>float</em>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.resources.ResourceVector.is_satisfied\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">is_satisfied</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">usage</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.resources.ResourceVector.is_satisfied\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Compare supplied slot, byte and token usage with the supplied limits.</p>\n<p>A dimension is skipped when either value is None. Bandwidth, compute\nand noise are not checked; this is not the full formal protocol order.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>usage</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#reckon.core.resources.ResourceVector\" title=\"reckon.core.resources.ResourceVector\"><em>ResourceVector</em></a>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>bool</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.resources.MemoryBudget\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">reckon.core.resources.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">MemoryBudget</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">max_slots</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">100</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">max_bytes</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">max_tokens</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">max_write_ops_per_window</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">max_read_ops_per_window</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">window_size</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">100</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.resources.MemoryBudget\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Memory-specific budget configuration for the Causal Memory Manager.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Variables<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>max_slots</strong> (<em>int</em>) – Maximum number of records to store</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>max_bytes</strong> (<em>int | None</em>) – Maximum total bytes</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>max_tokens</strong> (<em>int | None</em>) – Maximum total tokens</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>max_write_ops_per_window</strong> (<em>int | None</em>) – Write rate limit</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>max_read_ops_per_window</strong> (<em>int | None</em>) – Read rate limit</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>window_size</strong> (<em>int</em>) – Window size for rate limiting (in steps)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>max_slots</strong> (<em>int</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>max_bytes</strong> (<em>int | None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>max_tokens</strong> (<em>int | None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>max_write_ops_per_window</strong> (<em>int | None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>max_read_ops_per_window</strong> (<em>int | None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>window_size</strong> (<em>int</em>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.resources.MemoryBudget.to_resource_vector\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">to_resource_vector</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.resources.MemoryBudget.to_resource_vector\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Copy slot, byte and token limits, without constructing a formal protocol budget.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#reckon.core.resources.ResourceVector\" title=\"reckon.core.resources.ResourceVector\"><em>ResourceVector</em></a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n<section id=\"module-reckon.core.channels\">\n<span id=\"channels\"></span><h2>Channels<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-reckon.core.channels\" title=\"Link to this heading\">¶</a></h2>\n<p>Coarse-graining and record channels.</p>\n<p>Defines the observer interface through which agents interact with microstates.</p>\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.channels.CoarseGraining\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">reckon.core.channels.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">CoarseGraining</span></span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.channels.CoarseGraining\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Abstract interface for projecting a microstate to a macrostate at scale s.</p>\n<p>Implement project() and the corresponding fiber measure for the chosen\nstate spaces. MONAD’s model uses a deterministic measurable projection\nfollowed by a separate noisy record channel; this interface does not\nverify those mathematical assumptions.</p>\n<dl class=\"py property\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.channels.CoarseGraining.scale\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">abstract</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">property</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">scale</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">float</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.channels.CoarseGraining.scale\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>The scale parameter s for this coarse-graining.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.channels.CoarseGraining.project\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">abstractmethod</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">project</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">microstate</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.channels.CoarseGraining.project\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Project a microstate to a macrostate.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>microstate</strong> (<em>MicroState</em>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><em>MacroState</em></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.channels.CoarseGraining.fiber_measure\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">abstractmethod</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">fiber_measure</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">macrostate</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.channels.CoarseGraining.fiber_measure\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Compute μ(Γ_m) - the measure of the fiber/preimage.</p>\n<p>Used for Boltzmann entropy: S_B(m) = k log μ(Γ_m)</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>macrostate</strong> (<em>MacroState</em>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>float</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.channels.RecordChannel\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">reckon.core.channels.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">RecordChannel</span></span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.channels.RecordChannel\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Abstract record channel: M_s -&gt; Δ(Y_R)</p>\n<p>A noisy storage/measurement channel that maps observations\nto stored records under resource constraints.</p>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.channels.RecordChannel.encode\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">abstractmethod</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">encode</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">observation</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.channels.RecordChannel.encode\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Encode an observation into a record.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>observation</strong> (<em>MacroState</em>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><em>Record</em></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.channels.RecordChannel.decode\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">abstractmethod</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">decode</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">record</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.channels.RecordChannel.decode\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Decode a record back to an observation (possibly lossy).</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>record</strong> (<em>Record</em>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><em>MacroState</em></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.channels.RecordChannel.noise_level\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">abstractmethod</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">noise_level</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.channels.RecordChannel.noise_level\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Return the effective noise level ε_noise of this channel.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>float</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.channels.RecordChannel.cost\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">abstractmethod</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">cost</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">record</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.channels.RecordChannel.cost\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Return the resource cost (e.g., bytes) of storing this record.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>record</strong> (<em>Record</em>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>int</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n<section id=\"module-reckon.core.causality\">\n<span id=\"recorded-influence\"></span><h2>Recorded influence<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-reckon.core.causality\" title=\"Link to this heading\">¶</a></h2>\n<p>Resource-indexed direct influence between event pairs.</p>\n<p>The empirical relation records thresholded pairwise observations under\ndeclared resource constraints. Detectable influence from A to B and\nfrom B to C does not establish detectable influence from A to C.</p>\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.causality.DistinguishabilityMeasure\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">reckon.core.causality.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">DistinguishabilityMeasure</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">values</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.DistinguishabilityMeasure\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Measures for detecting causal influence.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.causality.CausalRelation\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">reckon.core.causality.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">CausalRelation</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">source</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">target</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">resources</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">distinguishability</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">measure</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">DistinguishabilityMeasure.TOTAL_VARIATION</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">threshold</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.1</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.CausalRelation\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Caller-supplied distinguishability for an event pair under resources R.</p>\n<p>The stored threshold classifies the supplied value; this object neither\nruns an intervention nor validates causal identification assumptions.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Variables<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>source</strong> (<em>str</em>) – The upstream event A</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>target</strong> (<em>str</em>) – The downstream event B</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>resources</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#reckon.core.resources.ResourceVector\" title=\"reckon.core.resources.ResourceVector\"><em>reckon.core.resources.ResourceVector</em></a>) – Resource constraints under which relation holds</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>distinguishability</strong> (<em>float</em>) – Measured distinguishability D(P(y|do(A=1)), P(y|do(A=0)))</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>measure</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.DistinguishabilityMeasure\" title=\"reckon.core.causality.DistinguishabilityMeasure\"><em>reckon.core.causality.DistinguishabilityMeasure</em></a>) – The divergence measure used</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>threshold</strong> (<em>float</em>) – The threshold η for detectability</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>source</strong> (<em>str</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>target</strong> (<em>str</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>resources</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#reckon.core.resources.ResourceVector\" title=\"reckon.core.resources.ResourceVector\"><em>ResourceVector</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>distinguishability</strong> (<em>float</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>measure</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.DistinguishabilityMeasure\" title=\"reckon.core.causality.DistinguishabilityMeasure\"><em>DistinguishabilityMeasure</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>threshold</strong> (<em>float</em>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py property\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.causality.CausalRelation.is_causal\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">property</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">is_causal</span></span><em class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"pre\">bool</span></em><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.CausalRelation.is_causal\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Compare the supplied value with threshold minus EPSILON (1e-9).</p>\n<p>Uses epsilon-based comparison to avoid floating-point precision issues.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.causality.DirectInfluenceRecords\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">reckon.core.causality.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">DirectInfluenceRecords</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">resources</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.DirectInfluenceRecords\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Observed direct-influence pairs under a fixed resource vector.</p>\n<p>Callers supply distinguishability values and thresholds. This collection\nchecks those recorded numbers; it does not run interventions or establish\nthat a protocol isolates an event’s causal effect.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>resources</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#reckon.core.resources.ResourceVector\" title=\"reckon.core.resources.ResourceVector\"><em>ResourceVector</em></a>)</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.causality.DirectInfluenceRecords.add_relation\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">add_relation</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">source</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">target</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">distinguishability</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">measure</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">DistinguishabilityMeasure.TOTAL_VARIATION</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">threshold</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.1</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.DirectInfluenceRecords.add_relation\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Add or update a causal relation.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>source</strong> (<em>str</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>target</strong> (<em>str</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>distinguishability</strong> (<em>float</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>measure</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.DistinguishabilityMeasure\" title=\"reckon.core.causality.DistinguishabilityMeasure\"><em>DistinguishabilityMeasure</em></a>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>threshold</strong> (<em>float</em>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.causality.DirectInfluenceRecords.causes\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">causes</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">source</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">target</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.DirectInfluenceRecords.causes\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Return the stored pair’s threshold decision, or False when the pair is absent.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>source</strong> (<em>str</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>target</strong> (<em>str</em>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>bool</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.causality.DirectInfluenceRecords.get_relation\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_relation</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">source</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">target</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.DirectInfluenceRecords.get_relation\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get the full relation object if it exists.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>source</strong> (<em>str</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>target</strong> (<em>str</em>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.CausalRelation\" title=\"reckon.core.causality.CausalRelation\"><em>CausalRelation</em></a> | None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.causality.DirectInfluenceRecords.upstream_of\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">upstream_of</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">target</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.DirectInfluenceRecords.upstream_of\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get all events that cause target.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>target</strong> (<em>str</em>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>list[str]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.causality.DirectInfluenceRecords.downstream_of\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">downstream_of</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">source</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.DirectInfluenceRecords.downstream_of\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get all events caused by source.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>source</strong> (<em>str</em>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>list[str]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.causality.DirectInfluenceRecords.all_events\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">all_events</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.DirectInfluenceRecords.all_events\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get all unique event identifiers in the relation.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>set[str]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.causality.DirectInfluenceRecords.check_transitivity\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">check_transitivity</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">alpha</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.05</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">multiple_testing_correction</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'none'</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.DirectInfluenceRecords.check_transitivity\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Report triples whose recorded direct influences do not compose.</p>\n<p>WARNING: The empirical estimator hat{preceq}_{R,n,alpha,M} is a noisy\ngraph. Pairwise significance does NOT compose: A-&gt;B and B-&gt;C at p&lt;alpha\ndoes NOT imply A-&gt;C is detectable at p&lt;alpha.</p>\n<p>This method reports violations as diagnostics, NOT failures.\nThe system does NOT assume closure.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>alpha</strong> (<em>float</em>) – Report metadata for the upstream significance level.</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>multiple_testing_correction</strong> (<em>str</em>) – Report metadata for the upstream\ncorrection method. This scan uses recorded pair thresholds.</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>TransitivityReport with violations and diagnostics</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.TransitivityReport\" title=\"reckon.core.causality.TransitivityReport\"><em>TransitivityReport</em></a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.causality.TransitivityViolation\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">reckon.core.causality.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">TransitivityViolation</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">triple</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">a_b_detected</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">b_c_detected</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">a_c_detected</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">a_b_distinguishability</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">b_c_distinguishability</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">a_c_distinguishability</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">a_c_threshold</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.TransitivityViolation\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Two detected edges whose endpoint pair is missing or below threshold.</p>\n<p>A missing endpoint pair has no distinguishability value. The reported\nthreshold then comes from the first edge of the path.</p>\n<p>This is a diagnostic, not a failure. The empirical estimator can violate\ntransitivity due to:\n- Stochasticity / finite sample size\n- Type I errors (false edges)\n- Type II errors (missing edges)\n- Selection bias (not all triples tested)\n- Multiple testing inflation</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>triple</strong> (<em>tuple[str, str, str]</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>a_b_detected</strong> (<em>bool</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>b_c_detected</strong> (<em>bool</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>a_c_detected</strong> (<em>bool</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>a_b_distinguishability</strong> (<em>float</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>b_c_distinguishability</strong> (<em>float</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>a_c_distinguishability</strong> (<em>float | None</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>a_c_threshold</strong> (<em>float</em>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.causality.TransitivityViolation.to_dict\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">to_dict</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.TransitivityViolation.to_dict\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Convert to dictionary for JSON serialization.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>dict</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.causality.TransitivityReport\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">reckon.core.causality.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">TransitivityReport</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">violations</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">violation_rate</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">total_triples_tested</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">alpha</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">multiple_testing_correction</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.TransitivityReport\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Report of triples whose observed direct influences do not compose.</p>\n<p>The diagnostic records the observed graph. Noise and finite samples\ncan affect that graph, and direct influence need not compose in principle.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>violations</strong> (<em>list[<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.TransitivityViolation\" title=\"reckon.core.causality.TransitivityViolation\">TransitivityViolation</a>]</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>violation_rate</strong> (<em>float</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>total_triples_tested</strong> (<em>int</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>alpha</strong> (<em>float</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>multiple_testing_correction</strong> (<em>str</em>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.causality.TransitivityReport.to_dict\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">to_dict</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.TransitivityReport.to_dict\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Convert to dictionary for JSON serialization.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>dict</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.causality.TransitivityReport.to_json\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">to_json</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">indent</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">2</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.TransitivityReport.to_json\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Convert to JSON string.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>indent</strong> (<em>int</em>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>str</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.causality.TransitivityReport.to_canonical_json\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">to_canonical_json</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.causality.TransitivityReport.to_canonical_json\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Encode finite report values under reckon.transitivity-report/v1.</p>\n<p>The profile sorts triples by Unicode code point, breaks repeated-triple\nties by their complete encoded values, and retains every entry. Object\nkeys are sorted; strings use ASCII escapes; separators have no spaces.\nHash the UTF-8 encoding without adding a newline. This does not mutate\nthe report or normalize event identifiers or numeric representations.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>str</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n<section id=\"module-reckon.core.credit\">\n<span id=\"credit-and-utility\"></span><h2>Credit and utility<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-reckon.core.credit\" title=\"Link to this heading\">¶</a></h2>\n<p>Credit Assignment Policies for observe().</p>\n<p>Calls the Rust kernel to distribute outcome credit\nto retrieved records. The credit is used to update utility estimates\nwhich inform retention decisions.</p>\n<dl class=\"simple\">\n<dt>Credit Policies:</dt><dd><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p>NONE: No credit assignment (standalone logging mode)</p></li>\n<li><p>SIMPLE: Equal credit to all retrieved records</p></li>\n<li><p>SHAPED: Credit weighted by the softplus of current utility</p></li>\n<li><p>ABLATION: Credit based on positive measured ablation deltas</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt>Credit Normalization:</dt><dd><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p>Active weights sum to one within floating-point rounding</p></li>\n<li><p>Measured non-positive effects can produce an all-zero vector</p></li>\n<li><p>The utility update enforces its own bounds</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt>Utility Update Rule:</dt><dd><p>u &lt;- (1 - eta) * u + eta * credit * outcome\nu = clamp(u, u_min, u_max)</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.credit.CreditPolicy\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">reckon.core.credit.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">CreditPolicy</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></span><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">values</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.credit.CreditPolicy\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Credit assignment policy for observe().</p>\n<p>Determines how outcome credit is distributed among retrieved records.</p>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.credit.CreditAssignment\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">reckon.core.credit.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">CreditAssignment</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">record_id</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">credit</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">policy</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.credit.CreditAssignment\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Credit assigned to a single record.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Variables<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>record_id</strong> (<em>str</em>) – ID of the record receiving credit</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>credit</strong> (<em>float</em>) – Credit amount (0-1, normalized per-observe call)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>policy</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#reckon.core.credit.CreditPolicy\" title=\"reckon.core.credit.CreditPolicy\"><em>reckon.core.credit.CreditPolicy</em></a>) – Policy used to compute this credit</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>record_id</strong> (<em>str</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>credit</strong> (<em>float</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>policy</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#reckon.core.credit.CreditPolicy\" title=\"reckon.core.credit.CreditPolicy\"><em>CreditPolicy</em></a>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.credit.CreditAssignment.to_dict\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">to_dict</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.credit.CreditAssignment.to_dict\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Convert to dictionary for serialization.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>dict</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.credit.CreditAssignment.from_dict\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">classmethod</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">from_dict</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">data</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.credit.CreditAssignment.from_dict\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Create from dictionary.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>data</strong> (<em>dict</em>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#reckon.core.credit.CreditAssignment\" title=\"reckon.core.credit.CreditAssignment\"><em>CreditAssignment</em></a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py function\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.credit.compute_credit\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">reckon.core.credit.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">compute_credit</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">record_ids</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">outcome</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">policy</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">utilities</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">ablation_deltas</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">shaped_scale</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">1.0</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.credit.compute_credit\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Compute credit assignments for retrieved records.</p>\n<p>SHAPED normalizes softplus(utility / shaped_scale) across retrieved records.\nMissing utilities default to 0.5 in the laboratory. A finite negative\noutcome changes the utility update, without changing the credit weights.\nABLATION normalizes positive measured ablation deltas. If every delta is\nabsent it falls back to equal credit; measured non-positive deltas earn\nno credit, even when no positive delta remains.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>record_ids</strong> (<em>List[str]</em>) – IDs of records that were retrieved</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>outcome</strong> (<em>float</em>) – Outcome value (e.g., reward, success indicator)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>policy</strong> (<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#reckon.core.credit.CreditPolicy\" title=\"reckon.core.credit.CreditPolicy\"><em>CreditPolicy</em></a>) – Credit assignment policy</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>utilities</strong> (<em>Dict[str, float] | None</em>) – Current utility values for SHAPED policy</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>ablation_deltas</strong> (<em>Dict[str, float] | None</em>) – Signed measured ablation deltas for ABLATION policy</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>shaped_scale</strong> (<em>float</em>) – Finite, positive scale for SHAPED policy</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>Normalized assignments, or zero weights for non-positive measured effects</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><em>List</em>[<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#reckon.core.credit.CreditAssignment\" title=\"reckon.core.credit.CreditAssignment\"><em>CreditAssignment</em></a>]</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<div class=\"doctest highlight-default notranslate\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">credits</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">compute_credit</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">... </span>    <span class=\"n\">record_ids</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"s2\">\"r1\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"r2\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"s2\">\"r3\"</span><span class=\"p\">],</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">... </span>    <span class=\"n\">outcome</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mf\">1.0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">... </span>    <span class=\"n\">policy</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">CreditPolicy</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">SIMPLE</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">... </span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"nb\">sum</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">credit</span> <span class=\"k\">for</span> <span class=\"n\">c</span> <span class=\"ow\">in</span> <span class=\"n\">credits</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"go\">1.0</span>\n</pre></div>\n</div>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py function\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.credit.update_utility\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">reckon.core.credit.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">update_utility</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">current_utility</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">credit</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">outcome</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">eta</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.1</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">u_min</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">u_max</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">1.0</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.credit.update_utility\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Update utility using exponential moving average.</p>\n<p>Formula: u &lt;- (1 - eta) * u + eta * credit * outcome\nThen clamp to [u_min, u_max].</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>current_utility</strong> (<em>float</em>) – Current utility value</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>credit</strong> (<em>float</em>) – Credit assigned to this record</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>outcome</strong> (<em>float</em>) – Outcome value (e.g., reward)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>eta</strong> (<em>float</em>) – Learning rate (default 0.1)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>u_min</strong> (<em>float</em>) – Minimum utility bound (default 0.0)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>u_max</strong> (<em>float</em>) – Maximum utility bound (default 1.0)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>Updated utility value, clamped to [u_min, u_max]</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>float</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<p class=\"rubric\">Example</p>\n<div class=\"doctest highlight-default notranslate\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"gp\">&gt;&gt;&gt; </span><span class=\"n\">update_utility</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">0.5</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">credit</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mf\">0.33</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">outcome</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mf\">1.0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"go\">0.483</span>\n</pre></div>\n</div>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n<section id=\"module-reckon.core.episode_context\">\n<span id=\"episode-context\"></span><h2>Episode context<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-reckon.core.episode_context\" title=\"Link to this heading\">¶</a></h2>\n<p>EpisodeContext for tracking retrieved records and credit assignment.</p>\n<p>The EpisodeContext uses Python’s ContextVar to provide thread-local/async-local\nstorage that tracks which records were retrieved during an episode step.\nThis enables automatic credit assignment when observe() is called.</p>\n<div class=\"highlight-python notranslate\"><div class=\"highlight\"><pre><span></span><span class=\"c1\"># In-process SDK mode (implicit context)</span>\n<span class=\"k\">with</span> <span class=\"n\">EpisodeContext</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">episode_id</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"ep_001\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span> <span class=\"k\">as</span> <span class=\"n\">ctx</span><span class=\"p\">:</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">records</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">manager</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">retrieve</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">query</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>  <span class=\"c1\"># auto-tracked</span>\n    <span class=\"c1\"># ... agent does something with records ...</span>\n    <span class=\"n\">credits</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">manager</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">observe</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">outcome</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mf\">1.0</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>  <span class=\"c1\"># uses ctx.retrieved_record_ids</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\"># Explicit Python context (the daemon has its own context IDs)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">ctx</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">EpisodeContext</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">episode_id</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"s2\">\"ep_001\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">records</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">manager</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">retrieve</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">query</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">context</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">ctx</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"n\">credits</span> <span class=\"o\">=</span> <span class=\"n\">manager</span><span class=\"o\">.</span><span class=\"n\">observe</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">outcome</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"mf\">1.0</span><span class=\"p\">,</span> <span class=\"n\">context</span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"n\">ctx</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</pre></div>\n</div>\n<dl class=\"py class\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">reckon.core.episode_context.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">EpisodeContext</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">id=&lt;factory&gt;</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">episode_id=''</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">step=0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">retrieved_record_ids=&lt;factory&gt;</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">created_at_ms=&lt;factory&gt;</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">ttl_ms=300000</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">_token=None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Context for tracking episode state and retrieved records.</p>\n<p>The EpisodeContext tracks which records were retrieved during an episode\nstep, enabling credit assignment when observe() is called. It supports\nimplicit ContextVar use and explicit passing of this context object.\nThe daemon has a separate registry addressed by context IDs.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Variables<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>id</strong> (<em>str</em>) – Unique context identifier (auto-generated UUID)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>episode_id</strong> (<em>str</em>) – Episode identifier for grouping</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>step</strong> (<em>int</em>) – Current step number within the episode</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>retrieved_record_ids</strong> (<em>List[str]</em>) – IDs of records retrieved in this context</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>created_at_ms</strong> (<em>int</em>) – Timestamp when context was created</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>ttl_ms</strong> (<em>int</em>) – Context lifetime; observe refuses expired contexts (default 5 minutes)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><ul class=\"simple\">\n<li><p><strong>id</strong> (<em>str</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>episode_id</strong> (<em>str</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>step</strong> (<em>int</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>retrieved_record_ids</strong> (<em>List[str]</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>created_at_ms</strong> (<em>int</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>ttl_ms</strong> (<em>int</em>)</p></li>\n<li><p><strong>_token</strong> (<em>Any</em>)</p></li>\n</ul>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext.current\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">classmethod</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">current</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext.current\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get the current context from ContextVar.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>The current EpisodeContext, or None if not in a context.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext\" title=\"reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext\"><em>EpisodeContext</em></a> | None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext.is_expired\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">is_expired</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext.is_expired\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Check whether elapsed time since creation exceeds this context’s TTL.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>True if the context has exceeded its TTL.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>bool</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext.add_retrieved_record\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">add_retrieved_record</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">record_id</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext.add_retrieved_record\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Add a record ID to the retrieved list.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>record_id</strong> (<em>str</em>) – ID of the retrieved record.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext.add_retrieved_records\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">add_retrieved_records</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">record_ids</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext.add_retrieved_records\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Add multiple record IDs to the retrieved list.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>record_ids</strong> (<em>List[str]</em>) – IDs of the retrieved records.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext.clear_retrieved_records\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">clear_retrieved_records</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext.clear_retrieved_records\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Clear the retrieved record IDs list.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext.advance_step\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">advance_step</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext.advance_step\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Advance to the next step, clearing retrieved records.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext.to_dict\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">to_dict</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext.to_dict\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Convert to dictionary for serialization.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>dict</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py method\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext.from_dict\">\n<em class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">classmethod</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></em><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">from_dict</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">data</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext.from_dict\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Create from dictionary.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>data</strong> (<em>dict</em>)</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext\" title=\"reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext\"><em>EpisodeContext</em></a></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py function\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.episode_context.get_current_context\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">reckon.core.episode_context.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">get_current_context</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.episode_context.get_current_context\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Get the current episode context.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>The current EpisodeContext, or None if not in a context.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext\" title=\"reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext\"><em>EpisodeContext</em></a> | None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py function\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.episode_context.set_current_context\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">reckon.core.episode_context.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">set_current_context</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">ctx</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.episode_context.set_current_context\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Set the current episode context.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Parameters<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><strong>ctx</strong> (<em><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext\" title=\"reckon.core.episode_context.EpisodeContext\">EpisodeContext</a> | None</em>) – The context to set, or None to clear.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-even\">Returns<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-even\"><p>Token that can be used to reset the context.</p>\n</dd>\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p><em>Any</em></p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n<dl class=\"py function\">\n<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"reckon.core.episode_context.clear_current_context\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">reckon.core.episode_context.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">clear_current_context</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#reckon.core.episode_context.clear_current_context\" title=\"Link to this definition\">¶</a></dt>\n<dd><p>Clear the current episode context.</p>\n<dl class=\"field-list simple\">\n<dt class=\"field-odd\">Return type<span class=\"colon\">:</span></dt>\n<dd class=\"field-odd\"><p>None</p>\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</dd></dl>\n\n</section>\n</section>\n",
